<title>USA: Citicorp sells $200 mln sub debt, yld +64bp.</title>
<headline>Citicorp sells $200 mln sub debt, yld +64bp.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Citicorp was priced on Wednesday via Goldman Sachs &amp; Co and Bear Stearns &amp; Co, according to market sources.</p>
<p>The notes were issued off of Citicorp's medium-term note shelf registration.</p>
<p>BORROWER CITICORP</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 7/01/2007</p>
<p>TYPE SUB NOTES     ISS PRICE 99.459  FIRST PAY DATE 1/01/98</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 7.076 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A  SPREAD 64 BPS     CALLABLE</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1672))</p>
</text>
